-- Facts restated in Boston Daily's own words with attribution. Every story carries its own photo; none was used in an earlier package or in the open 2026-11-09 and 2026-11-16 drafts (grepped content/ and seed/).
-- loc.gov and Wikimedia Commons were unreachable from the newsroom sandbox on this run. Photo URLs are Library of Congress tile URLs built from resource IDs confirmed by search (Carol M. Highsmith, Bain News Service and a historic stereograph, no known restrictions; the stereograph is flagged for rights confirmation). Editor: confirm each photo loads and matches its caption; the image check removes any that do not.
INSERT OR IGNORE INTO stories (id, slug, lane, type, section_slug, status, sensitive, headline, dek, body, byline, hero_image_url, hero_image_credit, hero_image_rights, source_system, source_ref, priority, is_lead_candidate, created_by, created_at, updated_at) VALUES ('bd-20261117-trump-manila-asean', 'trump-lands-in-manila-asean-quad-summit-asia-trip', 'newsroom', 'news_story', 'white-house', 'EDITORIAL_REVIEW', 0, 'Trump lands in Manila to open his Asia trip with a Quad meeting, a Thailand trade deal and an ASEAN summit', 'The president arrived in the Philippines on Tuesday, Nov. 17, for the 49th ASEAN Summit. A state visit with President Marcos follows on Wednesday, Nov. 18, before APEC talks in Shenzhen.', 'President Trump arrived in Manila on Tuesday, Nov. 17, at Ninoy Aquino International Airport, opening an Asia trip built around trade deals and meetings with U.S. allies, NBC Washington reported, citing the Associated Press. Philippine House Majority Leader Sandro Marcos, the son of President Ferdinand Marcos Jr., greeted him as he left Air Force One.

## The Manila schedule

Trump''s program for Tuesday, Nov. 17, included a meeting with leaders of the Quad, the grouping of the United States, Australia, India and Japan. It is the first Quad leaders meeting since he returned to the White House, according to the report. He was also set to sign a trade deal with Thailand, join a special summit with Southeast Asian leaders and attend a gala dinner as the summit''s guest of honor.

On Wednesday, Nov. 18, Marcos is to welcome Trump at Malacañang Palace with full military honors and a state banquet. Commercial deals in aviation, defense, energy and technology are expected to be announced.

## Protests and the next stop

Hundreds of protesters clashed with police in Manila on Sunday, Nov. 15, as they marched toward the summit venue, Democracy Now reported. They opposed Trump''s visit and a planned U.S.-led artificial intelligence hub under the Pax Silica initiative.

From Manila, Trump travels to Shenzhen, China, for the Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation summit. Democracy Now reported that Trump, Chinese President Xi Jinping and Russian President Vladimir Putin are scheduled to hold their first three-way summit there on Thursday, Nov. 19. Trump has also said he may meet North Korean leader Kim Jong Un, though no date has been given.', 'Boston Daily Staff', 'https://tile.loc.gov/image-services/iiif/service:pnp:stereo:1s30000:1s35000:1s35300:1s35363/full/pct:25/0/default.jpg', 'Sunset on Manila Bay, Philippine Islands (historic stereograph, file). Library of Congress Prints and Photographs Division (stereo.1s35363), no known restrictions; editor to confirm rights', 'public_domain', 'newsroom', 'content/2026-11-17.sql', 9, 1, 'newsroom-assistant', '2026-11-17T10:50:00.000Z', '2026-11-17T10:50:00.000Z');
